            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.494,
                0.619,
                0.557,
                0.637
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 8.3"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.655,
            0.884,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What shapes are these? Yes, these are our familiar squares and rectangles. But what makes them squares and rectangles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
            0.701,
            0.516,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider this rectangle ABCD."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.723,
            0.603,
            0.812
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The points A, B, C and D are the corners of the rectangle. Lines AB, BC, CD and DA are its sides. Its angles are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A}, \\angle \\mathrm{B}, \\angle \\mathrm{C}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and ∠D."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.814,
            0.603,
            0.905
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The blue sides AB and CD are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "opposite sides",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", as they lie opposite to each other. Likewise, AD and BC is the other pair of opposite sides."
            }
          ]
        },
